# SUBMIT - Run commands from a file

```text
SUBMIT procedure [arguments]
```

## Write a procedure

Put one CP/M command on each line of a .SUB text file. Use $1 for the
first argument, $2 for the second, and $$ for a literal dollar sign. For
example, save these two lines as CHECK.SUB:

```text
DIR $1
STAT $1
```

At the command prompt, run:

```text
SUBMIT CHECK D0:*.COM
```

## Supply responses

Ordinary procedure lines go to the command processor. To supply a
program's buffered console responses, place [XSUB](XSUB.HLP) before the
program and put its responses immediately after it. Single-key prompts
still read the keyboard.
